CAUSALITY EXPERIMENT ONLY. Not a Runtime fix or a general BCB lifetime policy.
Apply after cc-lifetime-probe.patch, on disposable x64 Debug test installations.
Retain only the observer-selected dirty BCB while its VACB is also marked dirty;
allow CcpFindBcb to find that selected BCB with zero pins. Keep pre-C2 FastFAT.
The exact predicate is a fixture filter, NOT a modified-no-write classification.
This deliberately lacks lazy-write retirement, purge/unmount integration and
concurrent writeback generations; VACB.Dirty is not a safe general release test.
Do not enable outside the isolated causality test. See CcLifetime.md.
With the same EXE and FastFAT: observer 0/128 per FAT, find-only 0/128,
keep-only 0/128, both 128/128. Executed private SMP kernel for both:
